radv/ps5: the rest of EglantinePS5's driver adaptations (tools/patch-radv-wsi.py DRIVER_ADAPTATIONS)

lead-mesh-12 took its memory fixes alone. These are the others EglantinePS5 applies to the same RADV: the command
stream not split inside an emulated task or mesh-as-compute draw; an upload buffer still in flight kept; a dispatch's
scratch written by the driver (EDEN_RADV_DISPATCH_SCRATCH); a mesh workgroup's primitive count by its primitive's
vertices; the mesh buffers' switch (EDEN_RADV_NO_MESH_BUFFERS); the NGG mesh path's publish wait; SPIR-V to NIR tried
again on a failure; empty pipeline cache objects refused; platform, queue and mapping failures reported.

